{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-flow","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Bash control flow, set -e/pipefail, and captured validator/redactor exits are central to this diff.","prompt_body":"Investigate the Bash execution paths around validator capture, redaction pipelines, result-env parsing, and fail handling. Look for places where set -euo pipefail, subshells, pipelines, or unset variables could bypass the documented exit contract or skip cleanup. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-state","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change adds exit 4 and retry state that must integrate with publish, sentinel, footer, and cleanup gates.","prompt_body":"Trace the Step 5c publish state machine across initial publish, validator defects, auto-repair retries, accept/proceed, cancel, and finalization. Check that stale .design-publish-result.env state cannot leak across attempts and that rc 4 never advances to summary, sentinels, footer, or cleanup before the retry loop settles. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"contract-drift","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Multiple script CLIs, docs, harnesses, and result-env key contracts are being changed together.","prompt_body":"Review cross-file contracts for removed review_budget, --force-validate, and --review-budget behavior, plus the new --skip-validate and VALIDATE_* result-env keys. Check that callers, usage text, docs, tests, and parser allowlists agree and that unknown-option behavior is intentional everywhere. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pause-publish","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Folding validation/redaction into design-publish risks bypassing pause/resume before side effects.","prompt_body":"Focus on pause/resume behavior around composed-plan publication and retries. Verify that pause checkpoints occur before validation, redaction, plan-block writes, diagrams, logs, renames, or reentry markers, and that issue/repo arguments are threaded consistently. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"redaction-path","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The publish driver now creates the redacted artifact and must not publish unredacted or empty content.","prompt_body":"Inspect the data path from composed-plan.md through redact-secrets.sh to composed-plan.redacted.md and then to plan publication. Look for any route that can publish unredacted content, publish an empty redacted body, continue after redactor failure, or expose sensitive content in logs or result env output. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
